==Trivia==
*Haniwanwan is based on a ''[[wikipedia:Haniwa|haniwa]]'', which were clay statues that were buried with the dead. ''Wan'' is the Japanese onomatopoeia for a dog's bark.
**Since it attacks by spinning, it could also be a reference to the ''haniwa''-like [https://nookipedia.com/wiki/Gyroid gyroids] from the ''Animal Crossing'' series; the name "Gyroid" is derived from the word ''gyrate'', meaning "rotate".
**Another possible reference is to the ''Final Fantasy'' series' [[wikia:finalfantasy:Cactuar|cactuar]], a green cactus with its arms in the same exact stance as Haniwanwan's. The cactuar resemblance would be greater if Haniwanwan had the face of an actual ''haniwa'' statue instead of a Doge.
*Visually, Haniwanwan is an enemy version of [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]].
*[[Relic Doge]] and Haniwanwan are the only [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemies whose [[Curse|curse]] abilities do not have a 100% chance to activate.
*It and [[Sir Rel]] are the only [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemies to have [[Single Attack]].
*It is tied with [[Othom]] for the lowest curse duration of all Relic enemies.

